{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "05 A paid model call",
  "description": "One paid model call from a mind: the gateway route, the worst-case estimate, who pays, budget checks, the reservation, the provider call, and settling the real cost. Lines were read at this repository's handover commit; if a line has moved, search the file for the step's function or symbol name.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2063,
      "title": "1. The route every mind calls",
      "description": "Minds call `/llm/v1/chat/completions` with their hive token (tour 04, step 14). If the request sets no output cap, the host sets 4096 tokens, so the estimate below is a true worst case."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/gateway.py",
      "line": 286,
      "title": "2. Gateway.estimate",
      "description": "First the local-only rule (tour 06). Local and mock providers skip budget admission (mock and zero-priced local models cost nothing; configured local prices are still recorded as spend, K53). A remote model with no configured price is refused (402 `unpriced_model`). `HIVE_ALLOW_UNPRICED=1` does not work around this today: it makes the estimate 0.0 (line 299), the reservation refuses a zero hold (`hive/core/cost_reservations.py` line 135), and the call ends 402 `reservation_refused` (`hive/core/app.py` line 2085). The flag fails closed; it is finding K12 in [FINDINGS.md](https://github.com/PhysixSNET/omegahive-schematics/blob/main/07-upgrade-path/FINDINGS.md). Price the model instead."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/gateway.py",
      "line": 332,
      "title": "3. The worst case",
      "description": "Input tokens are bounded by the UTF-8 byte length of everything billable, since a token covers at least one byte. Output is the requested cap. Several outputs per call (`n`, `best_of` > 1) and non-text content are refused before dispatch, because their cost has no bound."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/config.py",
      "line": 37,
      "title": "4. Prices live on the provider",
      "description": "A `Provider` is an OpenAI-compatible upstream with prices in USD per million tokens, per model or `*` as the default. `priced` (line 41) is what step 2 checks."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/gateway.py",
      "line": 265,
      "title": "5. Which key pays",
      "description": "A mind may be assigned a key from the keyring; if that key is gone, the call is refused (402 `key_unavailable`). Otherwise the provider's default key is used. The key id is recorded with the usage."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 1666,
      "title": "6. Which person pays",
      "description": "A person's own key: that person. Else the asker of an open Ask turn on this mind. Else the owner of an active session with it. Else the mind's owner, if a named person. Else the hive."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 1704,
      "title": "7. The budget check",
      "description": "A per-mind calls-per-minute ceiling stops runaway loops. A paid call needs a budget (0 means none, not unlimited) unless a hive total or the person's allowance covers it. Then every applicable rule and the hive's hard cap are checked against spend plus the worst case. Refusals are remembered for Health (`check_budget`, line 1687)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/budgets.py",
      "line": 263,
      "title": "8. Which limits apply",
      "description": "Scopes are the hive, the mind, its swarm, the key, and the paying person (unless on their own key). Explicit rules, automatic limits derived from a hive total, a swarm default and a member's monthly allowance all apply. `check` (line 294) refuses with 402 `spend_limit` and says which scope."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/cost_reservations.py",
      "line": 217,
      "title": "9. The budget snapshot",
      "description": "Inside the reservation transaction, the host gives the current limit and spend for each scope: the mind's lifetime budget, the hard total, and every applicable rule."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/cost_reservations.py",
      "line": 119,
      "title": "10. Reserve the worst case",
      "description": "In one SQLite write transaction: for every scope, recorded spend + money already held by other calls + this worst case must fit under the limit. The hold is stored with its scopes and subjects, so a rule added later still sees it. Only a hash of the request is kept, never its content. The chat route reserves and marks dispatched in one step (`dispatched=True`)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/gateway.py",
      "line": 340,
      "title": "11. The provider call",
      "description": "The local-only rule is checked again. Streaming is not supported yet. The mind's model name is split into provider and model, the paying key goes in the header, and the call is posted to the provider's `/chat/completions`. Cost is computed from the provider's reported token counts."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2090,
      "title": "12. A failed call keeps its hold",
      "description": "If the provider call fails or is cancelled, the money may still have been spent. The worst case stays held as an **unknown** liability (`hold_unknown`, line 122). Only a person resolves it later, with the real cost or a reason."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2109,
      "title": "13. Missing usage is not zero cost",
      "description": "If the answer has no valid token counts, the content is still delivered, but the hold stays unknown rather than being settled at $0."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/cost_reservations.py",
      "line": 170,
      "title": "14. Settle the real cost",
      "description": "The reservation becomes `settled` with the actual cost, and usage is recorded in the same transaction. A cost above the hold is recorded and flagged as an overrun, never hidden. A late answer after a person released the hold is recorded too."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 1735,
      "title": "15. Accounting",
      "description": "One `usage` row per call: mind, model, tokens, cost, key, swarm, the provider's resolved model, and the payer. The mind's `spent_usd` goes up and a `usage` event is published. The Ask conductor's calls use the same estimate, budget check and reservation (`hive/core/conductor.py` line 747)."
    }
  ]
}
